  "notes": [
   "The requirements are counted in high school 'Credits', not college units or hours; measure is recorded as 'units' and each units field holds those printed credits. The List of Courses tab prints contact hours for some courses (e.g., ABED 110 72 Hours), but these are not the credits used for the diploma requirements.",
   "The catalog prints 'Required Core Courses (110 Credits)' and 'Elective Cores Courses (50 Credits)' but prints no overall diploma total, so total_units is null (the 160 total is not computed).",
   "Each core sub-area states 'Minimum Required Credits'; these are recorded as choose_units blocks with that minimum. English Core (IHSS 100-102, 1-10 credits each, min 30) and Biological Sciences (four 2.5-credit courses, min 10) effectively require every listed course.",
   "Math Core (20 credits) and the other core areas are split into their printed sub-lists (Alegbra 1 [sic], Math, Biological Sciences, Physical Sciences, Economics, U.S. Government, U.S. History, World History), each recorded as its own block.",
   "The elective sub-headings (English, Humanities, Math, Natural Science, Social and Behavioral Science, Other Electives) print no separate minimums; all elective courses are recorded in one 50-credit choose_units block.",
   "The closed list writes 'IHSS174' without a space; the catalog prints 'IHSS 174'. This is treated as the same course, not a catalog addition.",
   "IHSS 109 appears twice in the closed list; it is placed once in the World History block.",
   "IHSS 154 and the non-IHSS Other Electives courses are not in the closed list and are marked as catalog additions.",
   "No program learning outcomes or named careers are printed for this program."
  ]
